<p>Russia held its annual Victory Day parade on Moscow’s Red Square on Saturday under heavy security, with President Vladimir Putin overseeing a ceremony smaller than in recent years and lacking tanks, missiles and other heavy military vehicles. President Trump announced a three-day Russia-Ukraine ceasefire on Friday, with reports saying Kyiv and Moscow also proclaimed or confirmed the pause. The parade marked the 81st anniversary of the Soviet victory over Nazi Germany, while Russia’s war in Ukraine has lasted more than four years and has been described in reports carrying Reuters as the deadliest European conflict since World War II. Meduza reported that the omission of military hardware made this the first such Moscow Victory Day parade since 2007; other accounts described it as the first in roughly two decades.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/sopwIiGcGUh9JlN5GWAa1SxZqgjy7-FQsUvqN3arybS1mGNb2wCfvvWEqjQZmqZfhCbvtaerW6hSzFYHH6v0HbqyPwxDNaKDtAyJy1m5OFodnEMqo0vCmvNsziwAiLY3d0ePtOR_dqRilDPemQ3bk1g-YelDhH0SB8BxYTzGesqEXTSeJFtfLqlZFE3gVsrsWT6r7hmNOONlvxHeMjI' alt='Russian servicemen stand in formation before the Victory Day military parade in Moscow on May 9, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Regional limits: A BBC Russian analysis said nearly 60 Russian cities removed military equipment from holiday programs or reduced it to retro columns, single vehicles or static displays.</li><li>Canceled parade: Perm Governor Dmitry Makhonin canceled the city’s Victory Day military parade for safety reasons, according to a report citing the Kyiv Independent.</li><li>Audience limits: Delfi reported that State Duma deputies were not invited to the Red Square stands and that spectator numbers on St. Petersburg’s Palace Square were cut tenfold.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kremlin and Russian Defense Ministry: Russian officials attributed the omissions to the security environment, with the Defense Ministry citing the current operational situation and Dmitry Peskov referring to a terrorism threat from Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/pasaulyje/6/2922200/politologas-apie-maskvos-parada-be-pompastikos-putinas-is-tiesu-bijo'>LRT</a>)</li><li>Ukraine: Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Red Square would be excluded from attacks, saying Kyiv would allow the ceremony to proceed rather than target it. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/09/ukraine-war-briefing-zelenskyy-hereby-decrees-moscow-can-hold-victory-day-parade'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Yevhen Mahda, Ukrainian political scientist: Mahda said Russia was panicking before the parade, that Ukraine had won that round of psychological warfare and that Europe had not yielded to Kremlin blackmail. (<a href='https://wiadomosci.dziennik.pl/swiat/artykuly/11244262,parada-bez-czolgow-i-strach-na-kremlu-politolog-rosja-panikuje-i-pod.html'>Dziennik</a>)</li><li>Abbas Gallyamov, political analyst and former Putin speechwriter: Gallyamov told Swedish radio that fears of attacks on Putin had increased and said more people in Russia, including previously loyal figures, believe Putin is leading the country into a dead end. (<a href='https://www.sverigesradio.se/artikel/9212645'>Sveriges Radio</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-russia-putin-scaled-back-victory-day-parade-paranoia-ukraine/'>Scaled-back Victory Day parade is a sign of Putin’s growing paranoia</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russia-holds-scaled-back-ww2-victory-parade-as-worries-over-war-in-ukraine-deepen'>Russia holds scaled-back WW2 victory parade as worries over war in Ukraine deepen</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/08/nx-s1-5810080/russias-victory-day-celebrations-are-dampened-by-ongoing-war-with-ukraine'>Russia&#x27;s Victory Day celebrations are dampened by ongoing war with Ukraine</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/09/world/e